    "name_ja": "リュウグウノツカイ",
    "scientific_name": "Regalecus glesne",
    "habitat": "mesopelagic",
    "order": 51,
    "notes": "Very long, scaleless, laterally compressed silver ribbon with small dark streaks; tiny protrusible mouth; a red dorsal fin runs the whole back and rises into a crest of long red rays over the head; paired red pelvic 'oars' hang below the head; no tail fin. Swims by rippling the dorsal fin with the body held straight, often hanging head-up."
